# Fork-safe Sift — 2 of 2: PRIVILEGED poster.
#
# Triggered when the build+render workflow (1 of 2) completes. Runs in the BASE
# repo context with a write token, so it does the ONE privileged thing — post the
# sticky comment from the trusted, pre-rendered artifact — and NOTHING ELSE.
#
# ⛔ FORBIDDEN — never do this in this job (or any pull_request_target job):
#     - uses: actions/checkout   with the PR head ref
#     - any build / compile / test / npm / make step
#   This job holds pull-requests: write in the base context; running fork-controlled
#   code here is remote code execution + secret exfiltration. The privileged job must
#   ONLY consume the artifact the unprivileged job already rendered. Keep the build in
#   1-of-2 (read-only token); keep the write here. Never cross the streams.
#
# ⚠️ DISABLED via the `.disabled` extension — GitHub ignores any non-`.yml`/`.yaml` file in
# .github/workflows/, so this poster is inert (it does NOT run, even once merged to main).
# THE FLIP — the founder-gated "LAST" act — is renaming this file to `sift-post.yml`, ONLY after:
#   (1) the Parse-Path / fuzz-ASan determinism gate is GREEN on the final pre-Marketplace dispatch,
#   (2) the engine-v<baseline> binary is published on sift-action (canon's render downloads it),
#   (3) baseline.ts degrades gracefully on a fork token (Hephaïstos — done, sift-action 3064eff), and
#   (4) the founder blesses it.
name: Sift (post)

on:
  workflow_run:
    workflows: ["Sift (build + render)"]
    types: [completed]

permissions:
  pull-requests: write     # post/update the sticky comment — the ONLY write this job needs
  actions: read            # download the triggering run's rendered artifact

jobs:
  sift-post:
    # Kept (the example's guard): with continue-on-error in 1-of-2 the render concludes `success`
    # even on a red build, so this still fires for red-build PRs — verify that on first live run.
    if: ${{ github.event.workflow_run.conclusion == 'success' }}
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      # NOTE: deliberately NO actions/checkout of the PR head and NO build step (see the FORBIDDEN
      # block above). `post` mode downloads the `sift-comment` artifact from the triggering run and
      # upserts the sticky comment — nothing else. poster.ts/artifact.ts enforce head_sha match + caps.
      - uses: CodeRoasted/sift-action@v1
        with:
          mode: post
          run-id: ${{ github.event.workflow_run.id }}
